  "notes": "Inputs 1-8 are rear combo XLR/jack. Inputs 1-2 are duplicated on the front; a front connection takes priority. The front panel description calls the front inputs combo XLR/jack, the specifications call them 6.35 mm jacks; jacks are listed here. Line Outputs 1/2 (A) and 3/4 (B) are the speaker pairs, 5-10 are line outputs. Two ADAT optical pairs, S/PDIF coax, word clock out (BNC), IEC power (not listed). Optional power inputs and the Kensington lock are not listed. Routing: inputs reach the computer via USB and the outputs via the Focusrite Control 2 mixer; computer playback reaches all outputs. Controls from the user guide, 'Front Panel': one gain control and SELECT 1-8 (the gain, 48V, INST, AIR, SAFE and LINK buttons act on the selected input; shown here once per input; AUTO and LINK not shown), DIM (-18 dB), MUTE, ALT, TALK, OUTPUT level and two headphone levels. Modelled: MUTE or ALT silence outputs 1 and 2. The front inputs 1 and 2 share the preamps with rear inputs 1 and 2; phantom power is shown for the rear XLR inputs. Assumption: levels at MIN are silent.",
